1
00:00:00,506 --> 00:00:02,716
(Leonard:)No, I'm having a moral crisis.

2
00:00:03,842 --> 00:00:08,642
(Sheldon:)Well, if it's of any help, I've read all
the great moral philosophers...

3
00:00:08,806 --> 00:00:10,846
(Sheldon:)...including Dr. Seuss.

4
00:00:13,227 --> 00:00:15,147
Oh, what the hell?

5
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:18,482
(Leonard:)I'm supposed to go see that
girl from the comic book store, Alice.

6
00:00:18,649 --> 00:00:22,739
(Leonard:)But I don't know if I should, because I'm
going out with Priya, but she's in India.

7
00:00:22,903 --> 00:00:27,573
(Sheldon:)All right.
So the topic at hand is sexual fidelity.

8
00:00:27,741 --> 00:00:30,621
(Sheldon:)Probably won't be relying
on Seuss here.

9
00:00:31,537 --> 00:00:33,827
AIthough One Fish Two Fish
Red Fish Blue Fish...

10
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:36,247
(Sheldon:)...might be surprisingly applicable.

11
00:00:37,251 --> 00:00:40,501
(Sheldon:)- Go on.
- Well, uh, they say at the end of your life...

12
00:00:40,671 --> 00:00:44,091
(Leonard:)...you regret the stuff you didn't do
more than the stuff that you did.

13
00:00:44,258 --> 00:00:48,388
(Leonard:)And I'm pretty sure Alice is the stuff
I wanna do.

14
00:00:49,847 --> 00:00:53,267
(Sheldon:)You know, the German philosopher
Friedrich Nietzsche...

15
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:56,773
(Sheldon:)...believed that morality
is just a fiction...

16
00:00:56,937 --> 00:00:59,607
(Sheldon:)...used by the herd of inferior
human beings...

